{{ 'ness-booking.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  Booking page.

  The prototype draws a three-step wizard here. It is deliberately not built:
  PLAN.md Decision #1 replaced it with a redirect to the studio's existing
  Acuity Scheduling page, so there is exactly one calendar to keep and no
  half-captured requests sitting in a theme with no backend.

  Everything else from the design survives — hero banner, "Plan your Perfect
  Style" steps, and the Booking Policy / Custom Wig & Drop-off cards. The
  wizard's card shell and its confirmation-state typography are reused for the
  panel that sends people to Acuity.

  No JavaScript: every control on this page is a link, so the page is complete
  the moment the HTML arrives.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    Booking URL, most specific first: a per-section override, then the
    site-wide theme setting (PLAN.md specifies a theme setting so every
    "Book a Session" control on the site reads one value), then the known
    Acuity link as a last resort so the button is never dead. This mirrors
    sections/ness-booking-banner.liquid exactly — the two must not drift.

    Kept on one line: inside a liquid tag every newline starts a new statement.
  endcomment
  assign booking_url = section.settings.booking_url | default: settings.acuity_url | default: 'https://nessclusive.as.me/schedule/6f74a017'
  assign cta_label = section.settings.cta_label | default: 'Book a Session'
  comment
    Falling back to the page's own title means the page can never render
    without an h1, whatever the merchant clears.
  endcomment
  assign hero_heading = section.settings.hero_heading | default: page.title | default: 'Book Nessclusive'
  assign steps = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'step'
  assign policy_lines = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'policy_line'
  assign dropoff_lines = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'dropoff_line'
  assign steps_id = 'ness-booking-steps-' | append: section.id
  assign panel_id = 'ness-booking-panel-' | append: section.id
  assign policy_id = 'ness-booking-policy-' | append: section.id
  assign dropoff_id = 'ness-booking-dropoff-' | append: section.id
-%}

<div class="ness-booking">
  {%- comment -%}
    Hero banner. The artwork is a real <img> rather than a CSS background so it
    can carry a srcset and be fetched eagerly — it is the first thing below the
    header on this template. The band's height is set in CSS and the image
    covers it, so any upload crops instead of distorting (Editability policy).

    `sizes` matches ness-booking-banner: the shell width less its side padding,
    which tops out at 1630px once the 1770px shell is reached.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="ness-booking__hero-band ness-shell">
    <div class="ness-booking__hero">
      <div class="ness-booking__hero-media">
        {%- if section.settings.hero_image != blank -%}
          {{
            section.settings.hero_image
            | image_url: width: 3000
            | image_tag:
              class: 'ness-booking__hero-image',
              alt: section.settings.hero_image.alt,
              widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 1900, 2400, 3000',
              sizes: '(min-width: 1770px) 1630px, calc(100vw - 40px)',
              loading: 'eager'
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Bundled prototype artwork as the default, so the page is never
            bare before a photo is chosen. Decorative: the headline over it
            carries the meaning.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <img
            class="ness-booking__hero-image"
            src="{{ 'ness-booking-bg.jpg' | asset_url }}"
            alt=""
            width="1600"
            height="1507"
            loading="eager"
          >
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <h1 class="ness-booking__hero-heading">{{ hero_heading | escape }}</h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The three steps. Wording is the prototype's, and it still describes the
    real flow — Acuity asks for a service, then a date and time, then
    confirmation. Every circle is filled: in the prototype the second and third
    were greyed to show wizard progress, and with no wizard a permanently grey
    step would read as unavailable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Throughout this section, aria-labelledby is emitted only when the heading
    it names is actually rendered. Pointing at an element that was never
    output leaves the region with an empty accessible name, which is worse
    than having none — same reasoning as ness-booking-banner.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if steps.size > 0 -%}
    <section
      class="ness-booking__steps ness-shell"
      {% if section.settings.steps_heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ steps_id }}"{% endif %}
    >
      {%- if section.settings.steps_heading != blank -%}
        <h2 class="ness-booking__steps-heading" id="{{ steps_id }}">
          {{- section.settings.steps_heading | escape -}}
        </h2>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        role="list" is not redundant: Safari drops list semantics from an <ol>
        whose list-style is none, which is exactly what the drawn circles
        require.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ol class="ness-booking__steps-list" role="list">
        {%- for block in steps -%}
          <li class="ness-booking__step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {%- comment -%}
              The circle is decoration — the <ol> already tells assistive tech
              this is step N of three, and announcing the digit twice is noise.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <span class="ness-booking__step-number" aria-hidden="true">{{ forloop.index }}</span>
            <p class="ness-booking__step-label">{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</p>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The booking call to action, standing where the wizard stood.

    The link is a plain same-tab navigation, matching ness-booking-banner. It
    is not forced into a new tab: a forced tab has to be announced to be
    accessible, and leaving that choice to the visitor is the behaviour the
    rest of the site already has.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <section
    class="ness-booking__book ness-shell"
    {% if section.settings.panel_heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ panel_id }}"{% endif %}
  >
    <div class="ness-booking__panel">
      <div class="ness-booking__panel-inner">
        <span class="ness-booking__badge">
          <svg
            width="38"
            height="38"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.7"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            aria-hidden="true"
            focusable="false"
          >
            <rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="16" rx="3"/>
            <path d="M3 10.5h18M8 3v4M16 3v4M7.5 14.5h3M7.5 17.5h6"/>
          </svg>
        </span>

        {%- if section.settings.panel_heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="ness-booking__panel-heading" id="{{ panel_id }}">
            {{- section.settings.panel_heading | escape -}}
          </h2>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.panel_body != blank -%}
          <p class="ness-booking__panel-body">{{ section.settings.panel_body | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.panel_note != blank -%}
          <p class="ness-booking__panel-note">{{ section.settings.panel_note | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="ness-booking__actions">
          <a class="ness-booking__cta" href="{{ booking_url | escape }}">{{ cta_label | escape }}</a>

          {%- if section.settings.secondary_label != blank -%}
            {%- capture secondary_url -%}
              {%- render 'ness-nav-url', destination: section.settings.secondary_destination -%}
            {%- endcapture -%}
            <a class="ness-booking__cta ness-booking__cta--secondary" href="{{ secondary_url }}">
              {{- section.settings.secondary_label | escape -}}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Booking Policy and Custom Wig / Drop-off. Each card is dropped entirely
    when it has no lines, rather than leaving a coloured panel with a heading
    and nothing under it.

    Lines are textareas rendered with `white-space: pre-line`, because the
    studio's policy is written as stacked clauses and reflowing it into a
    paragraph would change what it says.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if policy_lines.size > 0 or dropoff_lines.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="ness-booking__info ness-shell">
      {%- if policy_lines.size > 0 -%}
        <section
          class="ness-booking__card ness-booking__card--policy"
          {% if section.settings.policy_heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ policy_id }}"{% endif %}
        >
          {%- if section.settings.policy_heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="ness-booking__card-heading" id="{{ policy_id }}">
              {{- section.settings.policy_heading | escape -}}
            </h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="ness-booking__lines">
            {%- for block in policy_lines -%}
              <p class="ness-booking__line" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {{- block.settings.text | escape -}}
              </p>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </section>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if dropoff_lines.size > 0 -%}
        <section
          class="ness-booking__card ness-booking__card--dropoff"
          {% if section.settings.dropoff_heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ dropoff_id }}"{% endif %}
        >
          {%- if section.settings.dropoff_heading != blank -%}
            <h2 class="ness-booking__card-heading" id="{{ dropoff_id }}">
              {{- section.settings.dropoff_heading | escape -}}
            </h2>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="ness-booking__lines">
            {%- for block in dropoff_lines -%}
              <p class="ness-booking__line" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {{- block.settings.text | escape -}}
              </p>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </section>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Booking page",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Appointments are taken on Acuity, not on this page — every button here sends visitors to the Acuity link in Theme settings → Nessclusive. The wording, the banner photo, the three steps, and both policy cards are yours to edit. Layout, colours, and type are fixed by the design."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The page's own body text in Shopify admin is not shown on this template. Put everything you want visitors to read into the fields below."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Banner" },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "hero_image",
      "label": "Banner photo",
      "info": "Sits behind a purple wash and is cropped to fit, so nothing ever stretches. A wide landscape photo of at least 2400 × 900 works best."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hero_heading",
      "label": "Banner heading",
      "default": "Book Nessclusive",
      "info": "This is the page's main heading. Leave it empty and the page name is used instead."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Steps" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "steps_heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Plan your Perfect Style"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Booking button" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "panel_heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Book your appointment"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "panel_body",
      "label": "Body copy",
      "default": "Appointments are managed through our scheduler. Choose your service, pick a time that works for you, and confirm — it takes about a minute.",
      "info": "Around 150 characters is what the design was drawn for."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "panel_note",
      "label": "Small print",
      "default": "Your slot is held once the non-refundable deposit is paid. Please read the booking policy below before you book.",
      "info": "The quieter line under the body copy. Leave empty to hide it."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button label", "default": "Book a Session" },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "booking_url",
      "label": "Booking link (optional override)",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the site-wide Acuity link from Theme settings → Nessclusive. Only set this to send THIS page somewhere different."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "secondary_label",
      "label": "Second button label",
      "default": "Ask a question first",
      "info": "Leave empty to show the booking button on its own."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "secondary_destination",
      "label": "Second button goes to",
      "default": "contact",
      "options": [
        { "value": "contact", "label": "Contact page" },
        { "value": "faqs", "label": "FAQs page" },
        { "value": "all_products", "label": "All products" },
        { "value": "ready_to_ship", "label": "Ready to Ship" },
        { "value": "pre_order", "label": "Pre-Order" },
        { "value": "accessories", "label": "Accessories" },
        { "value": "home", "label": "Home page" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Policy cards" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "policy_heading",
      "label": "First card heading",
      "default": "Booking Policy"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "dropoff_heading",
      "label": "Second card heading",
      "default": "Custom Wig , Coloring & Drop off"
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 24,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "limit": 4,
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "What happens at this step",
          "default": "Select Your Desired Service",
          "info": "The number is added automatically from the order of the steps. The design was drawn for three."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "policy_line",
      "name": "Booking policy line",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "Deposit : ALL APPOINTMENTS REQUIRE A NON REFUNDABLE\nDEPOSIT TO SECURE YOUR SPOT.",
          "info": "Line breaks are kept exactly as you type them, so the policy stacks the way it is written."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "dropoff_line",
      "name": "Drop-off line",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "ALL FRONTALS, CLOSURES AND WIGS\nMUST BE DROPPED OFF 4-5 DAYS IN ADVANCE\nOR A FEE WILL BE CHARGED!",
          "info": "Line breaks are kept exactly as you type them."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "default": {
    "blocks": [
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "Select Your Desired Service" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "Select your preferable Time & date" } },
      { "type": "step", "settings": { "label": "Confirm and Get Ready" } },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": {
          "text": "Deposit : ALL APPOINTMENTS REQUIRE A NON REFUNDABLE\nDEPOSIT TO SECURE YOUR SPOT.\nREMAINING BALANCE MUST BE PAID IN CASH OR ZELLE\nON THE DAY OF YOUR APPOINTMENT."
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": {
          "text": "Reschedule : YOU CAN RESCHEDULE ONCE WITH YOUR DEPOSIT\nIN THE SAME MONTH RESCHEDULE UPTO 3 DAYS\nBEFORE YOUR ORIGINAL APPOINTMENT. NO EXCEPTIONS!"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": {
          "text": "Lateness : AFTER 10 MIN, YOU WILL BE CHARGED A $20 FEE.\nAFTER 20 MINS APPOINTMENT WILL BE CANCELLED"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": { "text": "Same day cancelation : DEPOSIT LOST AND 50% OF SERVICE CHARGED." }
      },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": { "text": "No call, No show : DEPOSIT LOST AND 50% OF SERVICE CHARGED." }
      },
      {
        "type": "policy_line",
        "settings": { "text": "** BY BOOKING YOU HAVE ACCEPTED AND AGREED TO THE TERM OF MY POLICY**" }
      },
      {
        "type": "dropoff_line",
        "settings": {
          "text": "For Order : TEXT 917-587-8962\nOR EMAIL INFO@NESSCLUSIVE.COM FOR ALL WIG ORDERS"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "dropoff_line",
        "settings": {
          "text": "ALL FRONTALS, CLOSURES AND WIGS\nMUST BE DROPPED OFF 4-5 DAYS IN ADVANCE\nOR A FEE WILL BE CHARGED!"
        }
      },
      { "type": "dropoff_line", "settings": { "text": "For Late Drop Off Policy:" } },
      { "type": "dropoff_line", "settings": { "text": "3 Days - $15 FEE," } },
      { "type": "dropoff_line", "settings": { "text": "2 Days - $25 FEE," } },
      { "type": "dropoff_line", "settings": { "text": "No 1 Day Drop off" } },
      { "type": "dropoff_line", "settings": { "text": "$40 FEE CHARGED FOR SAME DAY CUSTOMIZATION." } }
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
